 # Real-input native BEAMS through multiple-rest boundary
 
+Current CLI contract: [BEAMS epilog](BEAMS-EPILOG.md). The stage reports below describe the named historical checkpoint; current supported single-staff inputs can reach BEAMS.EPILOG. Phase snapshots retain their earlier completion flags.
+
 beams_pipeline::advance runs existing native initial candidates through the extension snapshot loop, late hooks, group formation, native rest mapping/detection/registration and shared graph synchronization. CLI beam-spots now emits later_beams, the actual latest supported substage, and common graph vertices/relations. Initial phase snapshots remain present. Registry and source candidate/group semantics are retained. BEAMS epilog/free glyph cleanup, LEDGERS/HEADS/rhythm/MusicXML are still pending and beams_complete/musicxml_complete remain false.
 
 native_rest_mapping consumes native GRID staff curves, measured thickness, specific interline, left/right abscissas and complete vLag then hLag sections. It supports one system and one default five-line staff whose native area is the full image, uses actual integer curve ordinates for StaffProjector sampling, and uses the original in-staff pitch formula 4*(2*y-bottom-top)/(bottom-top) at median endpoints. A beam center above the only staff's first line has no staff-at-or-above. Multi-system/multi-staff, unsupported area/edge geometry and outside-staff ledger pitch are explicit errors, not guessed association or false conversion. Source provenance bytecode for Staff/SystemInfo and StaffManager is preserved. The integrated eleven original conversion controls now derive endpoint pitches via this native mapping; six positive and five negative conversions still match. Two mapping contract tests cover curve samples, lag orientation/order, center pitch, multi-staff rejection and unsupported ledger range. Thirteen focused tests, fmt and all-targets Clippy pass.
